/T (Cultural norms and practices create additional obstacles for girls in accessing education, making it arduous for them to attend school and complete their studies. Early marriage, domestic responsibilities, and safety concerns are primary reasons why girls drop out of school, perpetuating gender inequality and further limiting their opportunities for personal growth and social empowerment.)
/E (Cultural norms and practices create additional obstacles for girls in accessing education, making it arduous for them to attend school and complete their studies. Early marriage, domestic responsibilities, and safety concerns are primary reasons why girls drop out of school, perpetuating gender inequality and further limiting their opportunities for personal growth and social empowerment.)
