554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (NRBC centers cater to underprivileged children who have temporarily dropped out of school. These centers are strategically located in isolated areas, such as deep forests or difficult terrains. NRBC teachers are recruited from the same community to ensure trust and familiarity, thereby facilitating in local languages. Engaging activities, including dance, drama, and games, help children bridge learning gaps. Once they reach the appropriate learning level, they seamlessly integrate into government residential schools for continued education. Table 02 shows that during FY 22-23, 12,939 children took remedial classes in 437 NRBC centers last year. 8,008 were mainstreamed to government schools. The rest of the children continued in the NRBCs.)
/E (NRBC centers cater to underprivileged children who have temporarily dropped out of school. These centers are strategically located in isolated areas, such as deep forests or difficult terrains. NRBC teachers are recruited from the same community to ensure trust and familiarity, thereby facilitating in local languages. Engaging activities, including dance, drama, and games, help children bridge learning gaps. Once they reach the appropriate learning level, they seamlessly integrate into government residential schools for continued education. Table 02 shows that during FY 22-23, 12,939 children took remedial classes in 437 NRBC centers last year. 8,008 were mainstreamed to government schools. The rest of the children continued in the NRBCs.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
