/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Transition data plays a crucial role in monitoring and supporting students' academic journey. It allows us to track their progress, identify potential dropouts, and gain insight into the challenges they face during transition periods. By identifying problematic areas, we can effectively communicate with the administration, enhancing the effectiveness of our program and interventions. Table 04 shows that almost 100% of children are transitioning successfully across grades. In FY 22-23, in Phase I blocks, 11,503 children in AWCs were eligible for grade 1 \(meaning they were around age 6\) and 100% of these children transitioned to primary. During the same year, 13,138 children in grade V were ready for the transition to upper primary and 99.95% of these children transitioned. )
/E (Transition data plays a crucial role in monitoring and supporting students' academic journey. It allows us to track their progress, identify potential dropouts, and gain insight into the challenges they face during transition periods. By identifying problematic areas, we can effectively communicate with the administration, enhancing the effectiveness of our program and interventions. Table 04 shows that almost 100% of children are transitioning successfully across grades. In FY 22-23, in Phase I blocks, 11,503 children in AWCs were eligible for grade 1 \(meaning they were around age 6\) and 100% of these children transitioned to primary. During the same year, 13,138 children in grade V were ready for the transition to upper primary and 99.95% of these children transitioned. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
