575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Learning Enrichment Program \(LEP\))
/E (Learning Enrichment Program \(LEP\))
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The Learning Enrichment Program focuses on enhancing the learning environment in government schools. It aims to revamp teaching approaches in Language, Math, Science, and Social Sciences by integrating innovations into the existing school system. LEP emphasizes six key aspects of learning: planning, teacher learning material \(TLM\), pupil organization, classroom culture, classroom transaction, and assessment. By employing various learning strategies, such as reading, writing, speaking, and comprehension exercises, the LEP aims to improve language and literacy skills, enhance imagination, and deepen subject knowledge. Moreover, teachers actively participate in designing their own TLM to align with the socio-cultural context of the classroom. 152 LEP centers were operational last year, reaching out to 5,523 children \(see Table 06\).)
/E (The Learning Enrichment Program focuses on enhancing the learning environment in government schools. It aims to revamp teaching approaches in Language, Math, Science, and Social Sciences by integrating innovations into the existing school system. LEP emphasizes six key aspects of learning: planning, teacher learning material \(TLM\), pupil organization, classroom culture, classroom transaction, and assessment. By employing various learning strategies, such as reading, writing, speaking, and comprehension exercises, the LEP aims to improve language and literacy skills, enhance imagination, and deepen subject knowledge. Moreover, teachers actively participate in designing their own TLM to align with the socio-cultural context of the classroom. 152 LEP centers were operational last year, reaching out to 5,523 children \(see Table 06\).)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
