/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Foundational Literacy and Numeracy \(FLN\) )
/E (Foundational Literacy and Numeracy \(FLN\) )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The FLN program, introduced in response to the NIPUN Bharat initiative, focuses on foundational literacy and numeracy for children in grades 1 to 3. This program specifically targets first-generation learners who lack support at home. These students often face language barriers and are taught by teachers who may be overburdened and lack resources and training.)
/E (The FLN program, introduced in response to the NIPUN Bharat initiative, focuses on foundational literacy and numeracy for children in grades 1 to 3. This program specifically targets first-generation learners who lack support at home. These students often face language barriers and are taught by teachers who may be overburdened and lack resources and training.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (To address these challenges, we have implemented a unique approach. We train locally educated volunteers who work alongside primary grade government teachers to deliver the FLN curriculum in schools. Each volunteer dedicates 2-3 hours every day to support the teachers and provide the necessary assistance. In addition, we ensure that the schools have access to appropriate teaching and learning resources, enhancing the quality of education provided.)
/E (To address these challenges, we have implemented a unique approach. We train locally educated volunteers who work alongside primary grade government teachers to deliver the FLN curriculum in schools. Each volunteer dedicates 2-3 hours every day to support the teachers and provide the necessary assistance. In addition, we ensure that the schools have access to appropriate teaching and learning resources, enhancing the quality of education provided.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
584 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Furthermore, we recognize that there is a significant language gap between the language spoken at home and the language used in the school setting. This poses a particular challenge for children from indigenous backgrounds, making it difficult for them to fully engage in the classroom. To tackle this issue, we have collaborated with the EkStep Foundation to develop a bridge language inventory of local and tribal languages. This inventory is accessible through the Government of India's Diksha app, enabling students to bridge the language gap and actively participate in their education.)
/E (Furthermore, we recognize that there is a significant language gap between the language spoken at home and the language used in the school setting. This poses a particular challenge for children from indigenous backgrounds, making it difficult for them to fully engage in the classroom. To tackle this issue, we have collaborated with the EkStep Foundation to develop a bridge language inventory of local and tribal languages. This inventory is accessible through the Government of India's Diksha app, enabling students to bridge the language gap and actively participate in their education.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
