609 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The 20 Pilot School Project was launched in collaboration between the University of Turku, the Tata Steel Foundation, and ASPIRE. Its implementation took place in November 2022, focusing on two blocks in Odisha: Danagadi and Sukinda, each comprising ten schools and a total of 1,685 children. The primary objective of this initiative is to integrate Finnish pedagogies into the science and math curricula of govt middle schools. \(See Table 08\))
/E (The 20 Pilot School Project was launched in collaboration between the University of Turku, the Tata Steel Foundation, and ASPIRE. Its implementation took place in November 2022, focusing on two blocks in Odisha: Danagadi and Sukinda, each comprising ten schools and a total of 1,685 children. The primary objective of this initiative is to integrate Finnish pedagogies into the science and math curricula of govt middle schools. \(See Table 08\))
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
610 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This project emphasizes both "In-Class Learning" and "Out-of-Class Learning" approaches. In the "In-Class Learning" environment, the classroom atmosphere is designed to allocate 20% of the time to instructors and 80% to students. On the other hand, "Out-of-Class Learning" focuses on utilizing children's time outside of the traditional classroom structure. This includes encouraging interactions with parents, observation, community engagement, and other activities that facilitate learning beyond the confines of the school setting.)
/E (This project emphasizes both "In-Class Learning" and "Out-of-Class Learning" approaches. In the "In-Class Learning" environment, the classroom atmosphere is designed to allocate 20% of the time to instructors and 80% to students. On the other hand, "Out-of-Class Learning" focuses on utilizing children's time outside of the traditional classroom structure. This includes encouraging interactions with parents, observation, community engagement, and other activities that facilitate learning beyond the confines of the school setting.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
611 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The project focuses on math and science for Grades 6 to 8, providing 2 hours per day with one hour before and after regular school hours. It breaks the misconception of math lacking imagination through practical, experiment-based content. Digital resources are integrated to enhance the learning experience, while a child-centric, activity-based approach encourages active student engagement. By incorporating guidance from the Finnish education system, the project aims to make learning tasks more innovative and culturally relevant.)
/E (The project focuses on math and science for Grades 6 to 8, providing 2 hours per day with one hour before and after regular school hours. It breaks the misconception of math lacking imagination through practical, experiment-based content. Digital resources are integrated to enhance the learning experience, while a child-centric, activity-based approach encourages active student engagement. By incorporating guidance from the Finnish education system, the project aims to make learning tasks more innovative and culturally relevant.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Ms. Sari-Isokyto Sinjoi and Ms. Mari Hanski Mari facilitated the online professional development of teachers for the 20 Pilot School Project. Ms. Sinjoi is a math and science teacher at the Teacher Training School in Rauma, Department of Teacher Education, while Ms. Mari is a math and physics teacher at the Teacher Training School in Turku. Their expertise and guidance provide valuable professional development opportunities for teachers, enhancing their teaching practices and effectively implementing the project's objectives.)
/E (Ms. Sari-Isokyto Sinjoi and Ms. Mari Hanski Mari facilitated the online professional development of teachers for the 20 Pilot School Project. Ms. Sinjoi is a math and science teacher at the Teacher Training School in Rauma, Department of Teacher Education, while Ms. Mari is a math and physics teacher at the Teacher Training School in Turku. Their expertise and guidance provide valuable professional development opportunities for teachers, enhancing their teaching practices and effectively implementing the project's objectives.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
