704 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Community Education Resource Centers serve as vital local institutions that are owned and managed by the community itself, addressing their educational, cultural, and critical information needs in the digital era. These centers play a pivotal role in bridging the digital divide and empowering remote rural communities by facilitating access to education and digital resources.)
/E (Community Education Resource Centers serve as vital local institutions that are owned and managed by the community itself, addressing their educational, cultural, and critical information needs in the digital era. These centers play a pivotal role in bridging the digital divide and empowering remote rural communities by facilitating access to education and digital resources.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
705 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (As part of our flagship Education Signature Program, 76 CERCs are currently operational in Odisha and Jharkhand. These centers are registered entities with dedicated community-owned bank accounts, ensuring financial transparency and sustainability. Equipped with computers, internet connectivity, printers, projectors, libraries, audio-visual content, arts and crafts materials, STEM learning resources, and screening capabilities for socially relevant films, talks, and seminars, the CERCs provide a wide range of resources to the communities they serve. The availability of such facilities enables access to digital empowerment and education. Communities can utilize the centers for online admissions, printing, photocopying, ticket booking, accessing certificates and records, and even job applications. )
/E (As part of our flagship Education Signature Program, 76 CERCs are currently operational in Odisha and Jharkhand. These centers are registered entities with dedicated community-owned bank accounts, ensuring financial transparency and sustainability. Equipped with computers, internet connectivity, printers, projectors, libraries, audio-visual content, arts and crafts materials, STEM learning resources, and screening capabilities for socially relevant films, talks, and seminars, the CERCs provide a wide range of resources to the communities they serve. The availability of such facilities enables access to digital empowerment and education. Communities can utilize the centers for online admissions, printing, photocopying, ticket booking, accessing certificates and records, and even job applications. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
706 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (They are integral components of the long-term sustainability and exit plan of the Education Signature Program. After the completion of the project, these centers will continue to serve as valuable resources for gram panchayats, youth groups, and self-help groups. These institutions will utilize the CERCs to update their knowledge and access information, ensuring the enduring impact of the program.)
/E (They are integral components of the long-term sustainability and exit plan of the Education Signature Program. After the completion of the project, these centers will continue to serve as valuable resources for gram panchayats, youth groups, and self-help groups. These institutions will utilize the CERCs to update their knowledge and access information, ensuring the enduring impact of the program.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
