739 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In the heart of Joda block, nestled in Keonjhar District, Odisha, resides a resilient 14-year-old girl named Risa Munda. Since 2018, she has sought refuge at the Girl's RBC alongside her 8-year-old sister. Risa's father, a former worker in the mining sector, and her mother, a resourceful homemaker who occasionally sells wood from the nearby jungle, have always strived to provide for their family's daily needs. However, Risa encountered difficulties in her studies, prompting her father to send her to her paternal grandmother's home in hopes of fostering academic focus.)
/E (In the heart of Joda block, nestled in Keonjhar District, Odisha, resides a resilient 14-year-old girl named Risa Munda. Since 2018, she has sought refuge at the Girl's RBC alongside her 8-year-old sister. Risa's father, a former worker in the mining sector, and her mother, a resourceful homemaker who occasionally sells wood from the nearby jungle, have always strived to provide for their family's daily needs. However, Risa encountered difficulties in her studies, prompting her father to send her to her paternal grandmother's home in hopes of fostering academic focus.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
740 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Yet, confined by the limitations and restrictions imposed there, Risa yearned for freedom. Driven by an unwavering spirit, one fateful day when her grandmother was absent, she embarked on a daring escape. Little did she know that her venture into the wilderness would lead her to a perilous journey lasting six harrowing days. With sheer determination, Risa sustained herself on wild fruits while enduring the thirst that ravaged her body. Fearful of jackals and pigs, she sought refuge on the precarious branches of trees, her only solace. On the sixth day, a faint sound reached her ears - the distant rumble of a passing train. This serendipitous encounter guided her towards a railway station, where compassionate strangers provided her with the assistance she desperately needed. Without a ticket, she surreptitiously boarded the train, hiding in the bathroom to evade the watchful eye of the ticket collector. Miraculously, amidst the bustling journey, a familiar face crossed paths with Risa. A kind lady whom she knew recognized her and became her guiding light, ensuring her safe return to the village she called home.)
/E (Yet, confined by the limitations and restrictions imposed there, Risa yearned for freedom. Driven by an unwavering spirit, one fateful day when her grandmother was absent, she embarked on a daring escape. Little did she know that her venture into the wilderness would lead her to a perilous journey lasting six harrowing days. With sheer determination, Risa sustained herself on wild fruits while enduring the thirst that ravaged her body. Fearful of jackals and pigs, she sought refuge on the precarious branches of trees, her only solace. On the sixth day, a faint sound reached her ears - the distant rumble of a passing train. This serendipitous encounter guided her towards a railway station, where compassionate strangers provided her with the assistance she desperately needed. Without a ticket, she surreptitiously boarded the train, hiding in the bathroom to evade the watchful eye of the ticket collector. Miraculously, amidst the bustling journey, a familiar face crossed paths with Risa. A kind lady whom she knew recognized her and became her guiding light, ensuring her safe return to the village she called home.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
